### 8.2 Editing model

Use structured reusable sections with typed server-side schemas, not an unrestricted page builder. Initial section types: hero video, introduction/CTA, category grid, product feature, image/text split, benefit list, service grid, approved testimonial group, FAQ, enquiry form, downloads, and related content. Each has stable IDs, schema version, editable values, and allowed visual/motion presets. Add page-specific form/account/commerce templates where needed.

Store page and global-setting drafts separately from the published revision. Support save, preview, publish, unpublish/archive, duplicate, revision history and restore. Use explicit capability checks for publishing. Make state and validation clear; warn about unsaved changes and handle conflicting edits with version checks. Server validation must reject invalid blocks and broken required relationships.

Preview must use an authenticated or short-lived scoped mechanism. It must not expose other drafts, privileged CMS credentials, customer data, or private attachments. Avoid preview tokens in analytics/logs/referrers. Expire and revoke them. Do not cache draft previews as public pages.

Publishing must update the public page and invalidate only affected public cache paths/tags. Use authenticated signed revalidation hooks with replay controls. Show processing/failure states and retry options. Never invalidate a global shared account/cart cache because those responses must not be shared in the first place.

### 8.3 Media management

Support upload, browse/search, alt text, title, usage relationships, replace asset, generation status, and deletion/archive rules. Public product media/manuals and private reference files/purchase evidence must have distinct storage access policies. An item being visible to staff in the media browser must not make it public.

Proposed configurable limits, subject to infrastructure review:

| Media class | Initial limit | Allowed baseline | Access |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Product/page image | 10 MB/file | JPEG, PNG, WebP; safe generated derivatives | Public only after publication |
| Manual | 20 MB/file | PDF, validated/scanned | Public after approval |
| Purchase evidence | 10 MB/file | PDF, JPEG, PNG | Private, authorised retrieval only |
| Hero/reference video | 250 MB source/file | MP4/WebM with verified codecs | Hero publication explicit; references private |
| Webfont | 2 MB/file | Licensed WOFF2 | Approved public font asset only |

Do not copy the old service form's displayed 1 GB proof-upload allowance. Distinguish staff source uploads from small customer evidence uploads. Verify video dimensions, duration, container/codec and size with a bounded media inspection job. Warn when hero input is not 1920 × 1080; reject publication of a non-16:9 hero unless an approved 16:9 rendition exists. Do not silently crop it.

Process large uploads with resumable/direct storage uploads and bounded worker jobs where infrastructure supports them. Validate completion server-side; a signed upload URL must not grant general bucket access. Quarantine files until validation/scanning completes. Limit CPU, memory, execution time and concurrency for image/video/font inspection and transformation. Run processors with minimum privileges and without unnecessary network access. A failed processor must leave a visible retryable state, not a public corrupt asset.

Prefer a clean SVG logo already reviewed as an application asset. If allowing uploaded SVG, sanitise it with a maintained SVG-specific tool and serve it safely; otherwise reject it or use a raster logo. Never allow uploaded HTML, executable scripts, or arbitrary inline markup. Treat font rights and font parsing as explicit checks.

