2. A hardware image linked to `/hardware/%20%E2%80%8E` instead of `/hardware/`.
3. Several footer service labels linked back to the homepage. Point them to relevant service content or an approved destination.
4. BETA gate opener names differed between B600/B550 and F600/F550. Obtain the approved model names before publishing.
5. Roller motor force values differed across pages, including 100N, 1000N, 1500N and 1800N references. Do not normalise them by guessing.
6. ARIA 121 catalogue content is not automatically equivalent to the old motor-pack shop product. Confirm any mapping, specifications and warranty independently.
7. The BETA Smart urgent link used a placeholder `#` target.
8. An emergency repair page repeated the enquiry DOM form ID. Generate unique field/form IDs when reusing a component.
